  "resource": {
    "dua": {
      "title": "Today's Dua",
      "arabic": "لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ، لَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ، وَهُوَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ. سُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ، وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ، وَلَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، وَاللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ، وَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ إِلَّا بِاللَّهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيمِ. رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي",
      "translation": "There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no deity except Allah, Allah is the Greatest. There is no power and no might except with Allah, the Most High, the Most Great. My Lord, forgive me.",
      "transliteration": "La ilaha illa Allah wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahu al-mulku wa lahu al-hamdu wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir. Subhan Allah, walhamdu lillah, wa la ilaha illa Allah, Allahu akbar, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah al-'Aliyy al-'Azim. Rabbi ighfir li.",
      "reference": "Sunan Ibn Majah 3878"
    },
    "hadith": {
      "arabic": "إِنَّهُ مَنْ قَامَ مَعَ الإِمَامِ يعنى في رمضان حَتَّى يَنْصَرِفَ كُتِبَ لَهُ قِيَامُ لَيْلَةٍ",
      "english": "Verily, whoever stands for prayer in Ramadan with the Imam until he is finished, it will be recorded as if he prayed the entire night.",
      "source": "Sunan al-Tirmidhī 806",
      "grade": "Sahih"
    }
  },
